    "topic": "Laws of Motion",
    "subtopic": "Newton's Laws & Friction",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "questionText": "A rod \ud835\udc34\ud835\udc35 of length 2 m is hinged at point \ud835\udc34 and its other end \ud835\udc35 is attached to a platform on which a block of mass \ud835\udc5a is kept. Rod rotates about point \ud835\udc34 maintaining angle \ud835\udf03= 30\u00b0 with the vertical in such a way that platform remains horizontal and revolves on the horizontal circular path. If the coefficient of static friction between the block and platform is \ud835\udf07= 0.1, then fin d the maximum angular velocity in rad s\u22121 of rod so that block does not slip on the platform (g = 10 ms\u22122)",
